Q. What is Amazon EC2 (Elastic Compute Cloud)?
A:	Amazon EC2 provides resize virtual servers in the cloud to run applications. It is scalable, cost-effective, and customizable, allowing users to launch and manage servers without physical hardware.
Example: Running a website on an EC2 instance instead of a physical server.

Q. What is AMI(Amazon machine Images)?
A: 	It is a template which contains all required software configuration like operating system , application server, and application to launch a virtual server.

Q. What is the Launch Template in AWS?
A:	A Launch Template in AWS is a saved configuration that contains all the settings needed to launch an EC2 instance.
It includes details like:
AMI (machine image)
Instance type (e.g., t2.micro)
Key pair
Security group
Storage (EBS)
User data (startup script)

